[
    {
        "content": "<p>In the following code the 1st union works but the 2nd and 3rd unions do not type-check:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⋃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⋃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"bp\">⋃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there a way to make <code>⋃ x ∈ xs, g x</code> work and return a <code>Finset Y</code>?</p>",
        "id": 615099362,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786062563
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe the notation is only defined for sets, but you can use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.biUnion#doc\">docs#Finset.biUnion</a>, or use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.foldl#doc\">docs#List.foldl</a> with the binary union</p>",
        "id": 615099533,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786062723
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The <code>⋃</code> notation definitely works for lists of sets, because the 1st <code>#check</code> in my example works.</p>",
        "id": 615099672,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786062879
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah because lists have <code>∈</code> defined, but the notation is for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.iUnion#doc\">docs#Set.iUnion</a> which will always result in a <code>Set</code>, and the nested expression must always be a <code>Set</code></p>",
        "id": 615099889,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786063082
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">help</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"⋃\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615100067,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786063230
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess I'll have to use <code>List.foldl</code>.</p>",
        "id": 615100092,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786063258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You could also do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">biUnion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFinset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">biUnion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615100155,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786063332
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Although the fold versions are pretty slick</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foldl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∪</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foldr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∪</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615100292,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786063474
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks!  It hasn't occurred to me to use the <code>·</code> notation.</p>",
        "id": 615100446,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786063592
    }
